                    {
                        "sense_id": "1894993f-c829-322e-96b6-6c849ff8580d",
                        "entry_id": "a06ca9aa-bd50-302e-9c08-3e5311fef38b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Uneasy; uncomfortable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9fb21850-c126-40c0-80b9-c204b04bf0ac",
                                "sense_id": "1894993f-c829-322e-96b6-6c849ff8580d",
                                "text": "If I did not view things in this light, my mind would be infinitely more disquieted than it is: for, if a crisis should arrive when a sense of duty, or a call from my country, should become so imperious as to leave me no choice, I should prepare for relinquishment, and go with as much reluctance from my present peaceful abode, as I should go to the tombs of my ancestors."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "714864b1-7f13-48dd-a3c6-d7f2be4b33ce",
                                "sense_id": "1894993f-c829-322e-96b6-6c849ff8580d",
                                "text": "Adèle, more and more disquieted, finally spoke to Margaret of her uneasiness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7bd78173-50f7-499d-aafb-bc651a368178",
                                "sense_id": "1894993f-c829-322e-96b6-6c849ff8580d",
                                "text": "\"They seemed at first very disquieted, \" reported Hunt, \"but we soon reassured them .[…]\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
